<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The watch app's theme, and the only reason it exists is the splash screen.

  Rejected by Play on 2026-09-08, Wear App Quality Guidelines: "Missing app icon
  in splash screen". The cause was not a wrong icon — it was that `:wear` had no
  theme AT ALL. No `<application android:theme>`, no themes.xml, nothing but a
  Translucent theme on the activation activity. With nothing declared, the
  launch window had no icon to show and came up bare.

  From Android 12 the system draws the splash itself and reads it from the
  theme, so the fix is a theme rather than a layout or a library: minSdk here is
  36, so `androidx.core:core-splashscreen` buys nothing and is not used.

  THE BACKGROUND IS BLACK BECAUSE THE GUIDELINE SAYS BLACK. Rejected a second
  time on 2026-09-10, and the wording is exact: "Your app does not show a
  48x48dp app icon on a black background during app startup." The first attempt
  put the mark on @color/ic_launcher_background — the blush the launcher icon
  uses — because reproducing the launcher icon looked like the coherent choice.
  It is not a matter of taste: Wear's branded launch specifies black, and a
  pink ground fails the check however well it matches the icon.

  The FOREGROUND layer is named rather than the adaptive `@mipmap/ic_launcher`
  because the system masks this drawable to a circle and would drop an adaptive
  icon's background layer, compositing the result over the colour above — the
  same picture drawn twice with only one of them under our control.

  windowBackground is black because this is a watch and the app's own surface is
  dark: without it the window flashes the platform default between the splash
  and the first Compose frame.
-->
<resources>
  <style name="Theme.BfgWatchFaces" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.NoActionBar">
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@android:color/black</item>
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
    <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/black</item>
  </style>
</resources>
